  owners used for normalized equal-weight averages;
- `Matrix.isDiag_diagonal`, `Matrix.PosDef.diagonal`, and `Matrix.diagonal_mul_diagonal` in
  mathlib, the canonical matrix-level diagonal API used by the surrounding Chapter 7 files.

Best owner abstraction:
- source-facing: the finite family of coordinate vectors, their box hull, and the averaged
  diagonal data appearing in Definition 7.35, with the textbook average vector `\hat a`;
- core/canonical: `B(g)`, `Finset.univ.centroid ℝ a`, `Matrix.diagonal`, `Matrix.IsDiag`, and
  `Matrix.PosDef`;
- bridge/view: the vector identity identifying the source average `\hat a = (1 / m) ∑ aᵢ` with
  the canonical centroid `Finset.univ.centroid ℝ a`, together with the induced diagonal /
